(window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY = window.IBALL_PERIODICAL_LIBRARY || {})["2026-08-31"] = {"meta":{"id":"2026-08-31","label":"2026 年 8 月 31 日 - 9 月 6 日","date":"2026-08-31","range":"2026-08-31|2026-09-06","theme":"英国","themes":["英国"],"sources":["The Guardian","BARRON’S","Economist"],"title":"More than 3,000 high street firms","titleZh":"（8.31—9.6）","counts":{"article":7,"paragraph":14,"vocab":22,"question":15,"qa":0,"original":5,"layout":0},"tabs":{"articles":true,"reading":true,"tests":true,"qa":false,"originals":true}},"articles":[{"file":"8.31—9.6 原文(1).docx","articles":[{"title":"More than 3,000 high street firms appear to be shells laundering money","titleZh":"","source":"The Guardian","publishedOn":"8.31","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"Up to £464m has “moved through” more than 3,000 UK shell companies branded as beauty and convenience stores but apparently operating in the money-laundering and terrorist financing sectors, a new analysis sets out."},{"index":2,"text":"The companies – some listed as hairdressers, barber shops and salons, others as mini-marts and corner shops – show “remarkably similar lifespans” of about six months despite their seemingly different purposes."},{"index":3,"text":"They are also “heavily concentrated in a small number of areas”, according to the research by the anti-money-laundering software provider SmartSearch."},{"index":4,"text":"The findings come amid increased scrutiny of the integrity of the UK company register, with many experts arguing that a proliferation of off-the-shelf businesses shows how bad actors are exploiting the system for money laundering and tax evasion."},{"index":5,"text":"This month, Andy Burnham announced plans to give councils new powers to stop betting and vape shops taking over their high streets, while in May the government said a new specialist unit would target “dodgy” retail outlets such as vape stores and sweet shops that are suspected of being used to launder £1bn of criminal money."},{"index":6,"text":"The topic was given more attention during a House of Commons Treasury committee meeting in June, when Paul Monaghan, the chief executive of the Fair Tax Foundation, told MPs: “There is a reason that we have a company register full of hundreds of thousands of fraudsters."},{"index":7,"text":"“The Insolvency Service has just recently shut down five illegal company service providers, which between them had set up 12,000 illegal companies in the UK, and we are only halfway through the year."},{"index":8,"text":"“We have got a problem in this country that the obsession to set it up cheap and quick creates all the other problems.”"},{"index":9,"text":"The SmartSearch analysis of Companies House records between 2016 and 2026 focused solely on the two business sectors of beauty and convenience stores."},{"index":10,"text":"It found 3,097 dissolved companies averaging 170 to 194 days of life, clustered into the same postcodes, the same registered addresses, and the same months of the year for incorporation and dissolution."},{"index":11,"text":"The data also showed how 83% of suspect hairdressing companies and 92% of suspect convenience stores were incorporated in the first and second quarters of each year, with more than half dissolved in the fourth quarter."},{"index":12,"text":"The cycle repeats annually across both sectors, the paper said, adding: “A single area of Cardiff contains 119 suspected companies on its own, across both sectors.”"},{"index":13,"text":"Phil Cotter, the chief executive of SmartSearch, said: “This is not a story about small businesses failing. It is a story about patterns that suggest a repeatable model of exploitation operating openly across UK high streets, and accelerating faster than the regulatory response has been able to catch. Companies House has made real progress since the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act came into force. But the register still reveals patterns that suggest the underlying activity is running ahead of the pace of reform.”"},{"index":14,"text":"The paper concludes: “The financial scale matters, and conservative modelling already suggests something between £310m and £464m has moved through these companies alone. Apply the same patterns across the other sectors named in the 2025 national risk assessment as high risk and the figure for the past decade likely sits above £1bn.”"}]},{"title":"Wildfires to rise by at least 39% in Europe by 2100 without action","titleZh":"","source":"The Guardian","publishedOn":"9.1","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"Wildfires are projected to burn 39% more of Europe by the end of the century even in the best-case scenario for stopping the planet from heating unless action is taken to manage them better, a study has found."},{"index":2,"text":"The increase in hot, dry and windy weather that leads to small fires turning into raging infernos is to engulf more of Europe as carbon pollution pushes temperatures higher. In the worst-case scenario the researchers modelled, in which global heating would reach 3.6C above pre-industrial levels, the burnt area would almost triple."},{"index":3,"text":"Improvements in fire management could moderate those increases by more than 70%, the study found, but not eradicate them entirely."},{"index":4,"text":"“Investments into fire management could help to a certain limit, but if we go on a path of high emissions … we still see strong increases in burnt area,” said Maik Billing, an ecosystem researcher at the Potsdam Institute for Climate Impact Research (PIK) and lead author of the study. “Fire management cannot replace climate mitigation.”"},{"index":5,"text":"The research comes as wildfires continue to ravage Europe, with large blazes hitting northern European countries such as the UK, Belgium and Germany after weeks in which France, Spain, Italy, Croatia and Greece battled monster infernos."},{"index":6,"text":"Across the EU, this fire season is on course to become the third-worst on record, behind 2025 and 2022, according to data published by the European Forest Fire Information Service yesterday."},{"index":7,"text":"More than 600,000 hectares have burned so far, with records broken for this time of year in Belgium, France and Slovakia."},{"index":8,"text":"The researchers, who compared the projected annual burnt area in Europe in 2070-2100 with modelled results for the period from 2000 to 2030, found that the increase in fire weather was the biggest driver of change."},{"index":9,"text":"In the optimistic scenario, in which global heating is capped at 1.8C above pre-industrial levels, a little above the current level of 1.4C, some regions showed moderate increases in fire weather while others experienced little change."},{"index":10,"text":"In the pessimistic scenario, however, with 3.6C of heating by the end of the century, the researchers found consistent worsening of fire weather across “virtually all of Europe”."},{"index":11,"text":"Scientists expect current policies to result in about 2.6C of global heating by the end of the century."},{"index":12,"text":"Using a second model, the researchers found that continued improvements in fighting fires could temper the effects of worsening fire weather, reducing burnt area by 92% in the cooler scenario compared with firefighting efforts remaining at today’s levels."},{"index":13,"text":"The researchers used the Human Development Index as a proxy for firefighting ability, but acknowledged that the rise of mega-fires had made it hard to extrapolate from past experience."},{"index":14,"text":"Improvements in fire suppression since the 1980s have reduced the number of fires and the area burnt in southern Europe, a study found this month, but the enthusiastic suppression of fires, even small ones, has paradoxically increased the residual fuel load."},{"index":15,"text":"This has allowed fires to develop to extreme levels when conditions are favourable, resulting in fewer but more ferocious fires."},{"index":16,"text":"Such monster fires hit France and Spain in late July this year, forcing a third of a million people from their homes as blazes raged with a force firefighters were unable to extinguish."},{"index":17,"text":"Víctor Resco de Dios, a forestry engineer at the University of Lleida, who was not involved in the study, said the fire season was often accompanied by an “unproductive blame game” – isolating only one of the two key factors whose interaction results in wildfires – and that the study was a reminder to move beyond scapegoating."},{"index":18,"text":"“The problem of wildfires wouldn’t be worsening if we were heading towards an ice age – instead of global warming,” he said. “And it would have been largely mitigated if our landscapes were like they were a century ago, with a much smaller forest area.”"}]},{"title":"Feeding AI: Data From A Bankrupt Airline Is Now Worth Millions","titleZh":"","source":"BARRON’S","publishedOn":"9.2","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"The race to build the most advanced artificial-intelligence tools has spawned a new market for real world data. It comes with both opportunities and pitfalls for investors."},{"index":2,"text":"Earlier this month, Google won an auction to purchase Spirit Airlines’ software code, internal messages, and financial and operational data for $10 million, according to filings from Spirit’s bankruptcy proceedings. Google hopes to use the data to improve its products and AI models, a spokesperson said."},{"index":3,"text":"That $10 million outlay for a busted airline’s data is just the tip of the iceberg. AI companies are vacuuming up corporate information of all sorts—a process that has taken on greater importance now that scraping the internet has become more legally fraught."},{"index":4,"text":"The demand for data is linked to how AI large-language models are created and refined. The computer systems ingest huge volumes of human information and use it to mimic human processes, such as writing reports, interpreting and responding to messages, and making recommendations. More data means more examples the model can pull from."},{"index":5,"text":"In response, public companies are weighing whether to license their data. And start-ups are opening marketplaces through which smaller enterprises can sell everything from contracts to email threads."},{"index":6,"text":"“Companies are sitting on decades of records that show how real work gets done, and that data is now some of the most valuable material for training and evaluating AI,” said a spokesperson from Mercor, an AI data start-up that made a $7.5 million bid in the Spirit auction."},{"index":7,"text":"The economics make perfect sense. The five largest cloud providers are spending a combined $800 billion in capital expenditures in 2026 to build data centers, and AI labs are paying hundreds of billions to use the facilities. Millions of dollars—with an “M”—mean very little to them when creating new AI tools, but that money can be a game-changer for data sellers."},{"index":8,"text":"The market appears to be picking up. In January, Cloudflare acquired HumanNative, a marketplace connecting content creators with AI developers. Two months later, News Corp, the owner of Barron’s publisher Dow Jones, struck a licensing deal with Meta Platforms, where the publisher sold access to its content for $50 million a year."},{"index":9,"text":"For smaller companies and even individuals looking to sell their data, an array of start-ups are emerging to broker deals."},{"index":10,"text":"Over a recent 11-day stretch, micro1, an AI data venture, committed more than $20 million to license operational data, said CEO Ali Ansari in a social media post this past week."},{"index":11,"text":"Investors can get in on the action, too. Barron’s made two stock picks last month based on the growing value of AI training data."},{"index":12,"text":"Reddit struck agreements with OpenAI and Google in 2024 to license conversations from its forums, bringing in an estimated $60 million a year from each lab. The social-media platform is now in negotiations with Google, and some investors and analysts expect a much larger deal."},{"index":13,"text":"John Wiley & Sons, a publisher of academic and technical literature, has also racked up big-name customers. The company’s licensing agreements with leading AI developers have generated more than $110 million since 2024. It also has collaborations with Amazon Web Services, Microsoft, Anthropic, and others."},{"index":14,"text":"The key for investors, and indeed companies, is pinpointing when data sales may do more harm than good."},{"index":15,"text":"Privacy is one challenge, particularly for consumer-facing businesses. Opera, the Norwegian web-browser company, has resisted selling data on those grounds."},{"index":16,"text":"“If we lose the users’ trust, if they think, ‘Oh, if we use the Opera browser, then they’re actually going to sell our data,’ then it’s probably not a wise move,” said Frode Jacobsen, chief financial officer at Opera, at an investor conference in January."},{"index":17,"text":"Disruption by AI is the other threat. If the labs use a company’s proprietary information to build something better, or at least more popular, they could siphon away demand."},{"index":18,"text":"“Our data is really the crown jewels of the future,” said Gary Morrison, CEO of hostel booking platform Hostelworld Group, in a conference call last month. “It is everything that we know about profiles, about bookings, about events, about people you’re meeting, what you’re talking about.”"},{"index":19,"text":"But companies like Hostelworld, and indeed Reddit and John Wiley, will have to survive in an AI-dominated world whether they like it or not. That means many more executives will have to decide how much “the crown jewels” are worth. August 24, 2026 | BARRON’S"}]},{"title":"Frozen fish","titleZh":"","source":"Economist","publishedOn":"9.3","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"Some species thrived during the last ice age. Sabre-toothed cats, giant ground sloths, woolly mammoths and woolly rhinos all did pretty well. Others, however, were seriously inconvenienced—among them the chum salmon of north-western North America, which frequently found the rivers leading to and from their inland spawning grounds icebound."},{"index":2,"text":"For those cut off in the sea, this was a nuisance. They had to make alternative arrangements, by seeking other, more accessible bodies of fresh water in which to lay their eggs. Those cut off on the land side, though, were stuck. And it was assumed until recently that because they were unable to complete the marine part of their life-cycle, they died out."},{"index":3,"text":"Not so, it turns out. A study published recently in Quaternary Research by Patrick Martin, an avid fisherman with a sideline as an amateur scientist, has employed genetics to show that some of the left-behinds not only endured, but thrived."},{"index":4,"text":"Pacific chum salmon range around that ocean’s rim from Japan and the Koreas to the coast of Oregon. Naturally, there is genetic variation in such a widespread population. Some of this variation is, though, so extreme that it has left researchers baffled. Three particular hot spots are around Kodiak island and nearby Cook inlet, in Alaska, and in the Salish sea between British Columbia and Washington state."},{"index":5,"text":"Intriguingly, it is not only the fishes’ genetics that differ, but also their behaviours. Most salmon migrate from the sea into fresh water to spawn in autumn or winter. The Salish sea population does so in summer. Similarly, salmon generally spawn in rivers. One of the Cook inlet populations, by contrast, does so in a lake."},{"index":6,"text":"Isolation over periods of thousands of years is well understood to drive evolution. This is obvious on small islands, such as the Galápagos. But walls of ice can isolate, too. With this in mind, Mr Martin speculated that the Kodiak, Cook and Salish salmon are genetically different from their neighbours because they got trapped, and survived, in glacial lakes."},{"index":7,"text":"Between 23,000 and 15,000 years ago glaciers created a lake on Kodiak island, with an area of 1,000 square kilometres and a depth of 300 metres. Glacial lakes also formed in valleys around the Olympic mountains of modern-day Washington state. To test his hunch, Mr Martin therefore convened a team of ichthyologists and geologists from the University of Washington and America’s National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration to analyse the genes of 32,817 specimens from 310 populations around the Pacific rim."},{"index":8,"text":"One question that needed an answer was whether the unusual genetics could be explained by a few salmon from Asia having taken a wrong turn and introduced their DNA into their North American cousins. The aberrant populations, however, bore no close relation to their Asian kin. Instead, the team proposes that the ancestors of these survived the ice age isolated in freshwater lakes, where they went their own sweet evolutionary ways."},{"index":9,"text":"During this period, Mr Martin and his colleagues argue, the fish rejigged their behaviour to treat the lakes they were trapped in like miniature oceans, complete with migrating up glacial streams feeding the lakes to spawn. That rejigging then persisted, at least in part, when the ice dams melted and the fish were liberated into the sea."},{"index":10,"text":"At least some of chum salmon’s genetic peculiarities are thus, presumably, the drivers of their unusual behaviours. But others could be relics of physiological adaptations to the stress of a life confined to fresh water in a species that normally spends much of its existence in the briny. That is of interest to evolutionary biologists. It may also intrigue conservationists, for genetic diversity is a good insurance against extinction and these odd salmon populations have diversity in spades. And fish farmers may take notice as well, if they are thinking about trying to raise salmon in colder waters or even freshwater lakes, where sea lice are absent and infectious pathogens less common. August 29TH- September 4TH ｜Science & technology"}]},{"title":"Marching across borders","titleZh":"","source":"Economist","publishedOn":"9.4","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"It was a smuggling operation to make your skin crawl. At Nairobi airport earlier this year, Kenyan authorities discovered more than 2,200 African harvester ants hidden in a man’s luggage. Most were packed inside small plastic tubes plugged with damp cotton, designed to keep the ants alive for weeks while they made it to their recipients, collectors in China. In April the smuggler was sentenced to a year in prison. His conviction followed a series of similar cases, including the arrest last year of two Belgian teenagers carrying around 5,000 ants."},{"index":2,"text":"A global craze for pet ants has fuelled a booming black market in live queen ants. An African harvester queen can sell for more than $200 in the black market (it costs barely $3 in Kenya). The country has become a hub for illegal trading because it has abundant populations of the species, alongside established smuggling networks that have long trafficked wildlife."},{"index":3,"text":"Ant-keeping became a popular pastime during the pandemic as people searched for indoor hobbies. Enthusiasts keep colonies in transparent formicariums—miniature “ant cities”—where they watch the insects dig tunnels and forage for food. Social media has helped turn the pastime into a global phenomenon. YouTube channels such as AntsCanada, which has more than 7m subscribers, narrate the stories of individual colonies like nature documentaries, from queens founding new nests to battles with rival species."},{"index":4,"text":"Most ant-keeping is perfectly legal. Specialist dealers breed the insects and sell them in licensed shops. But demand for rare and exotic ants has outpaced legal supply. African harvester ants are especially prized because they are among the world’s largest ant species and display complex social behaviours, making them “the tigers of the ant world”, says Dino Martins, an entomologist and evolutionary biologist based in Kenya."},{"index":5,"text":"Scientists worry that removing large numbers of ants could damage Kenyan ecosystems. Traffickers target queens because each colony has just one breeding female. She typically lives for 25 years and can produce a colony of thousands of workers. Ants play a crucial role in east Africa’s savannahs. As they forage, they collect and disperse grass seeds, helping maintain the diverse grasslands on which much wildlife depends. The ants’ vast underground nests add oxygen to the soil and create nutrient-rich hotspots where plants grow more easily. Meanwhile many other animals, such as pangolins, feast on the ants themselves."},{"index":6,"text":"Authorities are scrambling to stop the illegal exodus. Kenya Wildlife Service has pushed for tougher penalties and stepped up inspections at airports. But conservationists say the recent seizures are probably only the tip of the anthill. And interceptions address the trade only after the damage has been done. Alongside tougher enforcement, Mr Martins argues, authorities should educate collectors and local communities about the insects’ ecological importance. Unless demand falls, smugglers will find new ways to keep ants marching across borders. August 29TH- September 4TH ｜Middle East & Africa"}]},{"title":"Film-going frenzy","titleZh":"","source":"Economist","publishedOn":"9.5","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"To many grown-ups, the cartoon film “Niu Lai” would be 86 minutes of torture. Yet in recent days cinemas across China have been packed with older audiences happily enduring its crudely animated depiction of a bullock’s dream about motherly love and threatening predators. No matter that the film is excruciatingly slow-paced, with long seconds of silence as its characters merely blink. On a typical day in late August earnings at the box office were the seventh highest in China, just behind a new Hollywood blockbuster, “Spider-Man: Brand New Day”. The cartoon has become a meme-driven frenzy."},{"index":2,"text":"Western audiences have turned trashy films into cult classics: “The Room”, an American film released in 2003, became so notorious for its bad acting and appalling script and set design that audiences flocked to see it for laughs. “Niu Lai”, which is the bullock’s name (it means “the bull is coming”), has a similar attraction: a copy of it on YouTube, apparently filmed in a Chinese cinema with a mobile phone, drew more than 1.1m views before being deleted. The chuckles of the Chinese audience (the film is not supposed to be funny) are clearly audible."},{"index":3,"text":"Yet in a country where, unlike in Western countries, the government plays a big role in making, financing and shaping the narratives of films, the popularity of “Niu Lai”—an independent production by a mother-and-son team on a shoestring budget—is a remarkable phenomenon. Young people have flooded China’s social media with comments that often go beyond mere catcalling. On Weibo, one of the most popular platforms, posts with the hashtag “Niu Lai” have been viewed more than 170m times: well over the count (100m) for the hashtag of China’s currently hottest movie: “Once Upon a Time in the Middle East”. That one is a big-budget state-backed film that officials have been organising people to watch because of its heart-warming tale of a Chinese cook’s heroism amid a destructive American invasion of an Iraq-like country."},{"index":4,"text":"Despite deliberate seat-packing, the number-one film does appear to be genuinely popular. But online commenters use “Niu Lai” in order to poke at the industry’s pouring money into films that aim to spread the Communist Party’s messages; they use star actors but are often second-rate. Viewers carp at online censors’ habit of suppressing negative views of these party-backed extravaganzas. “Anyone can point at ‘Niu Lai’ and call it trash,” wrote one Weibo user to his more than 1.5m followers, echoing a commonly expressed view. “But those beautifully packaged, mega-budget super-flops in the film industry—are we even allowed to criticise them?…Absolutely not. That’s why they aren’t even as good as ‘Niu Lai’.”"},{"index":5,"text":"Discomfiting though such commentary must be for officials, the phenomenon may have upsides for the government. Some netizens have poached the cartoon’s imagery to produce mini-videos suggesting that a bull run in the stock market is on its way. Officials love to promote optimism about the country’s faltering economy. Amid the bull craze, censors are standing back. August 29TH- September 4TH ｜China"}]},{"title":"Dead wait","titleZh":"","source":"Economist","publishedOn":"9.6","paragraphs":[{"index":1,"text":"Running 600km along the coast of the Atacama desert, from southern Peru to northern Chile, is a mass-burial site for the world’s oldest mummies. The Chinchorro, who lived on the strip of coast from 7000BC to 1000bc, and survived by hunting and fishing, were meticulous preservers of their dead. Almost everyone who died could be mummified, with no regard for social status. This, combined with the dry environment of the Atacama, has led to an odd situation: the world’s oldest deliberately preserved bodies are so numerous that they are creating problems."},{"index":2,"text":"Lately, more bodies have been emerging from the earth. César Borie is an archaeologist with Chinchorro Marka, an agency that Chile’s government has charged with the protection of the country’s Chinchorro archaeological sites. He studies a skeleton that he stumbled upon while walking around Caleta Camarones, a town near the city of Arica in northern Chile. “We find new remains exposed every time we come here,” he says, gently reburying the bones with his hands. “Keeping them under the soil until the conditions are right is the best we can do.”"},{"index":3,"text":"This is not a new phenomenon. Chinchorro mummies have been issuing from the ground since at least the early 20th century. Initial expeditions in 1917 transported mummies to museums around Chile, where experts preserved them for study. Archeologists also ran excavations until the 1990s."},{"index":4,"text":"But erosion caused by extreme winds and increasing human activity nearby has been accelerating the mummies’ exposure. The region has run out of space to receive the bodies and keep them preserved. It would take hundreds of trucks to distribute them all, says Mr Borie. “There is nowhere to keep the mummies in museums without exposing them to damaging light and temperatures,” says Veronica Silva, an anthropologist at the Natural History Museum in Santiago, Chile’s capital."},{"index":5,"text":"And so archaeologists keen to learn more about the Chinchorro’s months-long mummification rituals are having to study the bodies in situ, reburying them when they are finished. “Until we have the right technology, we prefer keeping them underground instead of excavating more,” says Camila Castillo, also of Chinchorro Marka. A new museum that is under construction south of Arica should help."},{"index":6,"text":"In 2021 UNESCO added the Chinchorro remains and their landscape to its list of world heritage sites. That presented a possible solution: developing the sites into a tourist attraction, and hosting many of the mummies there. But not everyone is happy with that. A small fishing community has illegally built makeshift homes in the Camerones valley within the site. UNESCO would like them to relocate, but they are not so keen. Meanwhile their numbers are growing, and their presence is increasingly damaging the remains."},{"index":7,"text":"The local mayor, Christian Zavala, has upped the tension by saying the mummies get more attention than his constituents. But some older residents like José Concha, who has lived in the area for more than 30 years, understand the economic opportunities they offer. “I’m becoming too old to go fishing,” he says. “I would love to become a tour guide to teach tourists about the mummies.”"},{"index":8,"text":"Ms Castillo says Chinchorro Marka hopes to raise money to set up a centre where the mummies can be studied and exhibited in collaboration with residents of Camarones. But if that is to work, the archaeologists will need to show that they care as much about Caleta Camarones’s future as they do about its past. August 29TH- September 4TH ｜The Americas"}]}]}],"reading":[{"file":"8.31 精读 (1).pdf","headline":{"title":"","titleZh":"公司","source":"","series":"考研那些事儿之英国系列"},"paragraphs":[{"index":1,"en":"Up to £464m has “moved through” more than 3,000 UK shell companies branded as beauty and convenience stores but apparently operating in the money- laundering and terrorist financing sectors, a new analysis sets out.","zh":"一项新分析指出，高达4.64亿英镑的资金“流经”3000多家英国空壳公司。这些公司对外标榜为美容店和便利店，但实际上却从事洗钱和恐怖主义融资活动。"},{"index":2,"en":"The companies – some listed as hairdressers, barber shops and salons, others as mini- marts and corner shops – show “remarkably similar lifespans” of about six months despite their seemingly different purposes.","zh":"这些公司——有些登记为美发店、理发店和美容院，另一些则是小型超市和街角商店——尽管经营目的看似不同，但它们的“存续周期”却惊人的相似，大约都为六个月。"},{"index":3,"en":"They are also “heavily concentrated in a small number of areas”, according to the research by the anti- money- laundering software provider SmartSearch.","zh":"集中在少数精英人物的手里。根据反洗钱软件公司SmartSearch的研究，这些公司还“高度集中在少数几个地区”。"},{"index":4,"en":"The findings come amid increased scrutiny of the integrity of the UK company register, with many experts arguing that a proliferation of off- the- shelf businesses shows how bad actors are exploiting the system for money laundering and tax evasion.","zh":"该研究结果出现之际，英国企业登记册的可信性正受到越来越严密的审查；许多专家认为，现成空壳公司的激增说明不法分子正利用该制度进行洗钱和逃税。"},{"index":5,"en":"This month, Andy Burnham announced plans to give councils new powers to stop betting and vape shops taking over their high streets, while in May the government said a new specialist unit would target “dodgy” retail outlets such as vape stores and sweet shops that are suspected of being used to launder £1bn of criminal money.","zh":"本月，安迪·伯纳姆宣布计划赋予地方议会新权力，以阻止博彩店和电子烟商店占领商业街；而在5月份，政府表示将成立一个新的专门部门，打击电子烟店和糖果店等“可疑”零售门店，这些店铺涉嫌被用来洗白10亿英镑的犯罪所得。"},{"index":6,"en":"The topic was given more attention during a House of Commons Treasury committee meeting in June, when Paul Monaghan, the chief executive of the Fair Tax Foundation, told MPs: “There is a reason that we have a company register full of","zh":"今年6月，在下议院财政委员会的一次会议上，这一话题受到了更多关注。公平税收基金会首席执行官保罗·莫纳汉对议员们表示：“我们的公司登记册里充斥着数十万诈骗分子，这是有原因的。”"},{"index":7,"en":"“The Insolvency Service has just recently shut down five illegal company service providers, which between them had set up 12,000 illegal companies in the UK, and we are only halfway through the year.","zh":"“英国破产局近期刚刚关停五家非法企业服务供应商，这五家供应商合计在英国注册了12000家非法公司，而今年才刚过一半。”"},{"index":8,"en":"“We have got a problem in this country that the obsession to set it up cheap and quick creates all the other problems.”","zh":"“我们国家存在一个问题：热衷于便宜、快捷地注册公司，而这滋生了其他问题。”"},{"index":9,"en":"The SmartSearch analysis of Companies House records","zh":"SmartSearch对2016年至2026年间公司注册处记录进行分析，并仅将研究目标锁定在两个商业领域：美容店和便利店。"},{"index":10,"en":"It found 3,097 dissolved companies averaging 170 to 194 days of life, clustered into the same postcodes, the same registered addresses, and the same months of the year for incorporation and dissolution.","zh":"分析发现，有3097家已注销的公司，平均存续时长为170至194天，它们有着相同的邮政编码、相同的注册地址，并且集中在一年相同的月份进行注册和注销。"},{"index":11,"en":"The data also showed how 83% of suspect hairdressing companies and 92% of suspect convenience stores were incorporated in the first and second quarters of each year, with more than half dissolved in the fourth quarter.","zh":"数据还显示，83%的可疑美发公司以及92%可疑便利店在每年第一和第二季度注册，其中超过一半会在第四季度完成注销。"},{"index":12,"en":"The cycle repeats annually across both sectors, the paper said, adding: “A single area of Cardiff contains 119 suspected companies on its own, across both sectors.”","zh":"报告称，这样的周期模式在这两个行业每年都重复，还补充提到：“仅加的夫的一片区域，这两个行业内就存在119家可疑公司。”"},{"index":13,"en":"not a story about small businesses failing. It is a story about patterns that suggest a repeatable model of exploitation operating openly across UK high streets, and accelerating faster than the regulatory response has been able to catch. Companies House has made real progress since the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act came into force. But the register still reveals patterns that suggest the underlying activity is running ahead of the pace of reform.”","zh":"SmartSearch首席执行官菲尔·科特表示：“这并非关乎小企业的倒闭。这关乎的是一种模式。它表明一种可重复的利用模式正在英国商业街上公开运作，并且它扩张的速度已经超过监管反应所能跟上的速度。自《经济犯罪和企业透明度法案》生效以来，公司注册处（在打击犯罪以及提升企业信息透明度方面）已经取得了实质进展。但登记册仍显示出一些趋势，表明暗地里的（洗钱等非法金融）活动的步伐仍跑在改革前面。”"},{"index":14,"en":"The paper concludes: “The financial scale matters, and conservative modelling already suggests something between £310m and £464m has moved through these companies alone. Apply the same patterns across the other sectors named in the 2025 national risk assessment as high risk and the figure for the past decade likely sits above £1bn.”","zh":"报告总结道：“资金规模很重要，保守模型已经表明，仅这些公司就流经了3.1亿至4.64亿英镑。如果将同样的模式应用于2025年国家风险评估中列为高风险的其它行业，那么过去十年的数字可能超过10亿英镑。”"}],"vocab":[{"term":"launder","head":"v. to move money that has been obtained illegally into foreign bank accounts or legal businesses so that it is difficult for people to know where the money came from Organized crime groups launder their profits through anonymous companies.","definition":"to move money that has been obtained illegally into foreign bank accounts or legal businesses so that it is difficult for people to know where the money came from Organized crime groups launder their profits through anonymous companies.","gloss":"洗（钱）有组织的犯罪极端利用匿名公司洗黑钱。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"set out","head":"phrase. to present ideas, facts, etc. in an organized way, in speech or writing (","definition":"to present ideas, facts, etc. in an organized way, in speech or writing (","gloss":"有条理地）陈述，阐明","example":"He set out his objections to the plan.","exampleZh":"他陈述了他对这个计划的反对意见。","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"lifespan","head":"n. the length of time that sth is likely to live, continue or function Worms have a lifespan of a few months.","definition":"the length of time that sth is likely to live, continue or function Worms have a lifespan of a few months.","gloss":"寿命；可持续年限；有效期蠕虫的寿命为几个月。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"concentrate","head":"v. /kɒnsntreɪt/ to bring sth together in one place Power is largely concentrated in the hands of a small elite.","definition":"/kɒnsntreɪt/ to bring sth together in one place Power is largely concentrated in the hands of a small elite.","gloss":"使…集中（或集合、聚集）权力主要","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲词汇"]},{"term":"integrity","head":"n. (formal) the state of being whole and not divided to respect the territorial integrity of the nation SYN unity","definition":"(formal) the state of being whole and not divided to respect the territorial integrity of the nation SYN unity","gloss":"完整；完好尊重该国的领土完整","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"proliferation","head":"n. the sudden increase in the number or amount of sth; a large number of a particular thing 大 attempts to prevent cancer cell proliferation","definition":"the sudden increase in the number or amount of sth; a large number of a particular thing 大 attempts to prevent cancer cell proliferation","gloss":"激增；增殖；增生；量的事物防止癌细胞扩散的努力","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"off- the- shelf","head":"a. dj. (of products) that can be bought immediately and does not have to be specially designed or ordered","definition":"dj. (of products) that can be bought immediately and does not have to be specially designed or ordered","gloss":"现成的；从货架直接取下买走的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"evasion","head":"n. the act of avoiding sb or of avoiding sth that you are supposed to do She's been charged with tax evasion.","definition":"the act of avoiding sb or of avoiding sth that you are supposed to do She's been charged with tax evasion.","gloss":"躲避；规避；逃避；回避她被控逃税。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"council","head":"n. a group of people who are elected to govern an area such as a city or county （ a city/town/district/borough council","definition":"a group of people who are elected to govern an area such as a city or county （ a city/town/district/borough council","gloss":"市、郡等的）政务委员会，地方议会市／镇／区／自治市政务委员会","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"vape","head":"n. an electronic device, similar to an E-CIGARETTE, that produces VAPOUR, usually containing NICOTINE, that you can","definition":"an electronic device, similar to an E-CIGARETTE, that produces VAPOUR, usually containing NICOTINE, that you can","gloss":"","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"take over","head":"phrase. to begin to have control of or responsibility for sth, especially in place of sb else Paul's daughter took over the job in 2017. 手","definition":"to begin to have control of or responsibility for sth, especially in place of sb else Paul's daughter took over the job in 2017. 手","gloss":"接替；接任；接管；接手【考研大纲词汇】保罗的女儿于 2017 年接这一工作。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":["考研大纲 词汇"]},{"term":"dodgy","head":"a. dj. seeming or likely to be dishonest","definition":"dj. seeming or likely to be dishonest","gloss":"狡猾的；狡诈的；可疑的","example":"He made a lot of money, using some very dodgy methods.","exampleZh":"他采用一些极其狡诈的手段赚了许多钱。","tags":[]},{"term":"fraudster","head":"n. a person who commits fraud That data could someday be sold on the black market to medical fraudsters.","definition":"a person who commits fraud That data could someday be sold on the black market to medical fraudsters.","gloss":"犯欺诈罪者；犯欺骗罪者这些数据有一天可能会在黑市上被卖给医疗欺诈者。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"insolvency","head":"n. a situation in which a person or a company is insolvent 无力 One year later, Eik bank declared insolvency and was taken over by the state. 一","definition":"a situation in which a person or a company is insolvent 无力 One year later, Eik bank declared insolvency and was taken over by the state. 一","gloss":"偿还，破产年后，Eik 银行也宣布倒闭，被国家接管。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"shut down","head":"phrase. to stop a factory, shop, etc. from opening for business; to stop a machine from working （","definition":"to stop a factory, shop, etc. from opening for business; to stop a machine from working （","gloss":"使）关张，停业，倒闭，","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"obsession","head":"n. the state in which a person’s mind is completely filled with thoughts of one particular thing or person in a way that is not normal Her fear of flying is bordering on obsession.","definition":"the state in which a person’s mind is completely filled with thoughts of one particular thing or person in a way that is not normal Her fear of flying is bordering on obsession.","gloss":"痴迷；着魔；困扰她怕乘飞机几乎到了不可救药的地步。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"dissolve","head":"v. to officially end a marriage, business agreement or parliament Their marriage was dissolved in 1999.","definition":"to officially end a marriage, business agreement or parliament Their marriage was dissolved in 1999.","gloss":"解除（婚姻关系）；终止（商业协议）；解散（议会）他们于 1999 年解除了婚姻关系。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"incorporation","head":"n. the process or fact of legally making a company into a corporation or part of a corporation But Delaware, the biggest state for incorporation, is on board, as is America's treasury secretary, Steven Mnuchin.","definition":"the process or fact of legally making a company into a corporation or part of a corporation But Delaware, the biggest state for incorporation, is on board, as is America's treasury secretary, Steven Mnuchin.","gloss":"公司注册但最大的企业注册州，特拉华州以及美国财政部长史蒂文·努钦都支持立法。","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"repeatable","head":"a. dj. that can be repeated","definition":"dj. that can be repeated","gloss":"可重复","example":"The Feynman technique breaks the learning process into four broad and repeatable steps.","exampleZh":"费曼技巧将学习过程分为四个广泛且可重复的步骤。","tags":[]},{"term":"exploitation","head":"n. the fact of using a situation in order to get an advantage for yourself （ exploitation of the situation for his own purposes","definition":"the fact of using a situation in order to get an advantage for yourself （ exploitation of the situation for his own purposes","gloss":"出于私利的）利用利用这种局势达到他自己的目的","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]},{"term":"underlying","head":"a. dj. important in a situation but not always easily noticed or stated clearly","definition":"dj. important in a situation but not always easily noticed or stated clearly","gloss":"根本的；潜在的；隐含的","example":"Unemployment may be an underlying cause of the rising crime rate.","exampleZh":"失业可能是犯罪率攀升的潜在原因。","tags":[]},{"term":"conservative","head":"a. dj. opposed to great or sudden social change; showing that you prefer traditional styles and values the conservative views of his parents","definition":"dj. opposed to great or sudden social change; showing that you prefer traditional styles and values the conservative views of his parents","gloss":"保守的；守旧的他父母的保守观念","example":"","exampleZh":"","tags":[]}]}],"tests":[{"file":"【福利】8.31 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","type":"reading","instructions":[],"passage":[],"items":[{"number":21,"stem":"According to Paragraphs 1 and 2, the suspect companies were similar in that they _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"operated legal beauty and convenience businesses for about six months before closing"},{"key":"B","text":"were branded as ordinary retailers but showed unusually short and similar lifespans"},{"key":"C","text":"were all registered by the same local councils in a small number of shop units"},{"key":"D","text":"moved more than £464m through a single Cardiff convenience store"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·首段现象识别","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 1-2","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：Up to £464m has “moved through” more than 3,000 UK shell companies branded as beauty and convenience stores but apparently operating in the money-laundering and terrorist financing sectors...","- 原文（Para.2）：The companies – some listed as hairdressers, barber shops and salons, others as mini-marts and corner shops – show “remarkably similar lifespans” of about six months despite their seemingly different purposes.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：偷换概念陷阱。这些公司 branded as 零售企业，但 apparently operating in money-laundering and terrorist financing sectors，不是合法经营后自然倒闭。","- 选项B（正确）：原文说明它们以美容和便利店身份出现，却呈现约六个月的 remarkably similar lifespans。B 项同时保留“表层零售身份”和“异常相似寿命”两个特征。","- 选项C（错误）：无中生有陷阱。原文说公司集中在少数地区，但没有说都由同一批地方议会注册， councils 是后文提出监管权力的主体。","- 选项D（错误）：细节拼接陷阱。£464m 是 3,000 多家公司合计金额的上限；Cardiff 某一区域有 119 家可疑公司，不是单一便利店流入全部金额。","【命题技巧】","- 表层与实质对比：branded as 与 apparently operating in 的落差是首段核心。","- 数字归属：总额、公司数、区域数量必须分别核对，不能跨句拼接。"]},{"number":22,"stem":"The author mentions the plans of Andy Burnham and the government in Paragraph 5 in order to _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"prove that local councils have already eliminated retail money laundering"},{"key":"B","text":"suggest that betting and vape shops are the only sources of criminal money"},{"key":"C","text":"show that official concern has begun to translate into targeted measures"},{"key":"D","text":"criticise the Treasury committee for ignoring high-street crime"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"[C]","analysis":["【题型】例证题·政策例证功能","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 5","【解析】","- 原文（Para.5）：This month, Andy Burnham announced plans to give councils new powers to stop betting and vape shops taking over their high streets...","- 原文（Para.5）：...while in May the government said a new specialist unit would target “dodgy” retail outlets such as vape stores and sweet shops that are suspected of being used to launder £1bn of criminal money.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：过度推理陷阱。计划和新专门单位说明开始应对，不能推出已经消除零售洗钱。","- 选项B（错误）：过度推理陷阱。betting shops 和 vape shops 是例子，原文还提到 sweet shops，且后文扩展到其他高风险行业。","- 选项C（正确）：该段承接 increased scrutiny：Burnham 计划赋予地方议会新权力，政府设立专门单位，都说明官方关注正转为有针对性的监管行动。","- 选项D（错误）：无中生有陷阱。下文 Treasury committee 会议进一步讨论该问题，作者没有批评它忽视犯罪。","【命题技巧】","- 政策例证服务观点：新权力与专门单位是证据，服务“监管关注度上升”这一观点。","- 时态与结果区分：announced plans 与 said 不能推出已彻底解决问题。"]},{"number":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 6 to 8 that Monaghan regards the UK's company-registration system as _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"too cheap and quick, thereby making fraudulent registration easier"},{"key":"B","text":"too strict for ordinary small businesses that need to incorporate quickly"},{"key":"C","text":"well protected because hundreds of thousands of fraudsters have been removed"},{"key":"D","text":"irrelevant to the illegal company-service providers shut down this year"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"[A]","analysis":["【题型】推理判断题·人物观点推理","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 6-8","【解析】","- 原文（Para.6）：Paul Monaghan...told MPs: “There is a reason that we have a company register full of hundreds of thousands of fraudsters.”","- 原文（Para.7）：The Insolvency Service has just recently shut down five illegal company service providers, which between them had set up 12,000 illegal companies in the UK...","- 原文（Para.8）：“We have got a problem in this country that the obsession to set it up cheap and quick creates all the other problems.”","分析：","- 选项A（正确）：Monaghan 明确把问题归结为 obsession to set it up cheap and quick，认为便宜快捷的注册便利制造了后续大量欺诈和非法公司问题。A 项准确概括其观点。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。他批评的是系统过于便捷易被滥用，不是过于严格妨碍小企业。","- 选项C（错误）：细节拼接陷阱。register full of fraudsters 和 Insolvency Service 关闭部分服务商说明问题严重、治理只是开始，不是系统已受良好保护。","- 选项D（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。非法公司服务提供商正是利用注册系统设立 12,000 家公司，与注册制度高度相关。","【命题技巧】","- 人物观点定位：直接引语中的因果关系是观点题的核心证据。","- 治理行动与制度评价区分：关闭服务商是补救动作，不等于制度本身没有漏洞。"]},{"number":24,"stem":"Which of the following is true about the SmartSearch findings in Paragraphs 9 to 12?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It examined all UK business sectors from 2016 to 2026 and found 3,097 still-active companies."},{"key":"B","text":"The suspect companies were generally incorporated in the second half and dissolved in the first quarter."},{"key":"C","text":"Less than half of suspect convenience stores were registered in the first two quarters of a year."},{"key":"D","text":"The companies often shared registered addresses and followed repeated seasonal cycles of registration and closure."}],"answer":"D","kicker":"[D]","analysis":["【题型】细节理解题·数据规律识别","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraphs 9-12","【解析】","- 原文（Para.9）：The SmartSearch analysis of Companies House records between 2016 and 2026 focused solely on the two business sectors of beauty and convenience stores.","- 原文（Para.10）：It found 3,097 dissolved companies averaging 170 to 194 days of life, clustered into the same postcodes, the same registered addresses, and the same months of the year for incorporation and dissolution.","- 原文（Para.11）：...83% of suspect hairdressing companies and 92% of suspect convenience stores were incorporated in the first and second quarters of each year, with more than half dissolved in the fourth quarter.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：细节杂糅陷阱。研究 focused solely on beauty and convenience stores，且 3,097 家是 dissolved companies，不是覆盖所有行业或仍在经营的公司。","- 选项B（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。多数公司在第一、二季度设立，超过一半在第四季度解散，B 项把时间方向颠倒。","- 选项C（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。92% 的可疑便利店在上半年注册，不是少于一半。","- 选项D（正确）：原文指出这些公司平均存活 170 至 194 天，集中在相同邮编、注册地址，并重复相同月份的设立与解散周期。D 项完整概括其规律性。","【命题技巧】","- 数据方向核对：第一二季度注册、第四季度解散是常被反向替换的考点。","- 研究范围限定：solely two sectors 与 2016-2026 决定研究对象边界。"]},{"number":25,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title for the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"High Street Revival: How Beauty and Convenience Stores Are Growing"},{"key":"B","text":"Shell Games: Suspicious Retail Firms Reveal a Repeatable Laundering Model"},{"key":"C","text":"Companies House Completed: Why Corporate Reform Has Ended Financial Crime"},{"key":"D","text":"Local Shopping: The Economic Value of Small Hairdressers and Corner Shops"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"[B]","analysis":["【题型】主旨大意题·最佳标题","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Full text","【解析】","- 原文（Para.1）：...more than 3,000 UK shell companies branded as beauty and convenience stores but apparently operating in the money-laundering and terrorist financing sectors...","- 原文（Para.13）：“It is a story about patterns that suggest a repeatable model of exploitation operating openly across UK high streets...”","- 原文（Para.14）：...£310m and £464m has moved through these companies alone...the figure for the past decade likely sits above £1bn.","分析：","- 选项A（错误）：反义干扰陷阱。文章不是写高街零售复苏，而是这些零售身份可能掩盖金融犯罪。","- 选项B（正确）：全文围绕 3,000 多家可疑空壳公司展开，通过相似寿命、地理集中、季节性注册解散和资金规模，说明一种公开运行且可复制的洗钱模式。B 项兼顾现象与实质。","- 选项C（错误）：过度推理陷阱。原文承认 Companies House 有进展，但强调 underlying activity is running ahead of the pace of reform，改革没有终结金融犯罪。","- 选项D（错误）：以偏概全陷阱。美容店和便利店只是伪装类别，文章不评价其正常经济价值。","【命题技巧】","- 现象与机制概括：最佳标题不能停留在零售店表层，应指向 shell/laundering model。","- 限定词保留：suspected/repeatable 与文中证据强度一致，避免绝对化。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语阅读理解大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。","如果对答案解析有疑惑，直接打开任何AI大模型（如Deepseek、Kimi等），上传该篇原文文档，然后复制粘贴对应的题目和选项，说清楚你的疑问，大模型会回应解释对应的问题。"]}]},{"file":"【福利】8.31检验题__完型填空(1).docx","type":"cloze","instructions":["Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)"],"passage":["The SmartSearch analysis of Companies House records between 2016 and 2026 focused solely on the two business sectors of beauty and convenience stores. It found 3,097 dissolved companies averaging 170 to 194 days of life, ____【11】____ into the same postcodes, the same registered addresses, and the same months of the year for incorporation and dissolution. The data also ____【12】____ how 83% of suspect hairdressing companies and 92% of suspect convenience stores were ____【13】____ in the first and second quarters of each year, with more than half ____【14】____ in the fourth quarter. The cycle repeats ____【15】____ across both sectors, the paper said, adding: “A single area of Cardiff contains 119 suspected companies on its own, across both sectors.”","Phil Cotter, the chief executive of SmartSearch, said: “This is not a story about small businesses ____【16】____. It is a story about ____【17】____ that suggest a repeatable model of ____【18】____ operating openly across UK high streets, and accelerating ____【19】____ than the regulatory response has been able to catch. Companies House has made real progress since the Economic Crime and Corporate Transparency Act came into force. But the register still reveals patterns that suggest the underlying activity is running ____【20】____ the pace of reform.”"],"items":[{"number":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"separated"},{"key":"B","text":"clustered"},{"key":"C","text":"divided"},{"key":"D","text":"scattered"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (clustered)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·分布语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第2句","【解析】","[A] separated（分开）：强调被分开，方向与 same postcodes 和 same addresses 相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] clustered（聚集）：clustered into the same postcodes 表示“集中在相同邮政编码区域”，与后文三个 same 形成呼应。正确答案。","[C] divided（划分）：可与 into 搭配，但强调人为分类，不能自然说明公司在地理和时间上的聚集。搭配干扰。","[D] scattered（分散）：强调散布各处，与高度集中的调查发现矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"concealed"},{"key":"B","text":"estimated"},{"key":"C","text":"showed"},{"key":"D","text":"denied"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (showed)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·数据语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] concealed（隐瞒）：与数据给出具体百分比的方向相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] estimated（估计）： percentages 本身是精确结果，不是粗略估计。程度差异干扰。","[C] showed（显示）：The data showed how... 表示“数据显示了……”，引出具体发现。正确答案。","[D] denied（否认）：与研究报告呈现证据的语境矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"incorporated"},{"key":"B","text":"dissolved"},{"key":"C","text":"inspected"},{"key":"D","text":"licensed"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (incorporated)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·公司生命周期","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] incorporated（注册成立）：be incorporated in the first and second quarters 表示公司在第一、二季度注册成立。正确答案。","[B] dissolved（解散）：后文说超过半数在第四季度解散，此处若再填 dissolved 会造成时间矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[C] inspected（检查）：语法可通，但不是公司注册时间点的生命周期动作。语义场干扰。","[D] licensed（获得许可）：与季度分布的注册语境无关。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"registered"},{"key":"B","text":"inspected"},{"key":"C","text":"incorporated"},{"key":"D","text":"dissolved"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (dissolved)","analysis":["【题型】上下文语义·时间链条","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第3句","【解析】","[A] registered（注册）：公司注册发生在前文的第一、二季度，不是第四季度的结果。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] inspected（检查）：无法体现公司生命周期终结。语义场干扰。","[C] incorporated（注册成立）：与前文已说明的注册时间冲突。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] dissolved（解散）：more than half dissolved in the fourth quarter 表示“超过半数在第四季度解散”，与年度循环呼应。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"irregularly"},{"key":"B","text":"annually"},{"key":"C","text":"randomly"},{"key":"D","text":"gradually"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (annually)","analysis":["【题型】副词辨析·频率语义","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 1, 第4句","【解析】","[A] irregularly（不规则地）：与 repeatable model 和重复周期矛盾。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] annually（每年）：The cycle repeats annually 表示“这一循环每年重复”，与各季度固定变化对应。正确答案。","[C] randomly（随机地）：随机现象无法形成可识别的年度模式。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] gradually（逐渐地）：只能表示速度，不能说明周期按年重复。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"succeeding"},{"key":"B","text":"investing"},{"key":"C","text":"failing"},{"key":"D","text":"expanding"}],"answer":"C","kicker":"C (failing)","analysis":["【题型】动词辨析·情感方向","【难度】⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第1句","【解析】","[A] succeeding（成功）：与 not a story about 之后的负面判断方向不符。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] investing（投资）：可与小企业搭配，但文段不是讨论经营投入。语义场干扰。","[C] failing（失败）：not a story about small businesses failing 表示“这不是小企业倒闭的故事”。正确答案。","[D] expanding（扩张）：方向与困境语境相反。逻辑方向干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"patterns"},{"key":"B","text":"accidents"},{"key":"C","text":"disputes"},{"key":"D","text":"records"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (patterns)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·上下文语义","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] patterns（模式）：与后文 repeatable model 及全文的周期性数据呼应。正确答案。","[B] accidents（偶然事件）：偶发事件不能说明可重复模式。语义场干扰。","[C] disputes（争议）：文段未讨论法律或商业纠纷。语义场干扰。","[D] records（记录）：数据来自记录，但能让模型显形的是 patterns，而非记录本身。近义干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"competition"},{"key":"B","text":"charity"},{"key":"C","text":"innovation"},{"key":"D","text":"exploitation"}],"answer":"D","kicker":"D (exploitation)","analysis":["【题型】名词辨析·感情色彩","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] competition（竞争）：中性商业行为，与洗钱和系统性滥用语境不符。感情色彩干扰。","[B] charity（慈善）：方向完全相反。感情色彩干扰。","[C] innovation（创新）：带正面色彩，不能概括非法利用。感情色彩干扰。","[D] exploitation（利用、剥削）：a repeatable model of exploitation 表示“可重复的滥用模式”。正确答案。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"slower"},{"key":"B","text":"faster"},{"key":"C","text":"later"},{"key":"D","text":"harder"}],"answer":"B","kicker":"B (faster)","analysis":["【题型】副词辨析·比较关系","【难度】⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第2句","【解析】","[A] slower（更慢）：与问题加速发展的语境相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[B] faster（更快）：accelerating faster than 表示“比……加速更快”。正确答案。","[C] later（更晚）：比较时间先后，不比较发展速度。语义场干扰。","[D] harder（更难）：可修饰动作难度，但不是 speed comparison。搭配干扰。","— — — — — — — — — — —"]},{"number":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ahead of"},{"key":"B","text":"short of"},{"key":"C","text":"clear of"},{"key":"D","text":"mindful of"}],"answer":"A","kicker":"A (ahead of)","analysis":["【题型】固定搭配·速度关系","【难度】⭐⭐⭐⭐","【定位】Paragraph 2, 第4句","【解析】","[A] ahead of（领先于）：running ahead of the pace of reform 表示问题发展速度快于改革速度。正确答案。","[B] short of（不足）：running short of 表示“缺少”，不能与 the pace of reform 构成合理比较。搭配干扰。","[C] clear of（避开、远离）：running clear of 表示避开，方向与监管落后于问题的含义相反。逻辑方向干扰。","[D] mindful of（注意到）：表示态度，不表示活动速度超过改革速度。语义场干扰。","— — — — — — — — — —","本文档由我们自研的考研英语完型填空大模型生成。该模型基于近10年考研英语真题进行训练。我们会根据同学们的反馈持续优化模型能力。","本文档为【福利】，不提供答疑服务，欢迎大家自行交流使用。","【两个常见问题】","随着AI技术的不断进步，通过知识投喂和持续训练，大模型已逐渐具备模仿真题命题风格的能力。这份文档正是这一尝试的成果。它仅作为福利提供给大家，起到辅助检验的作用。你可以根据自身需要选择使用，如果有所顾虑，完全可以不用。"]}]}],"qa":[],"originals":[{"kind":"source","label":"原文","file":"8.31—9.6 原文(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":154247,"date":"2026-08-31","range":"2026-08-31|2026-09-06","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.31—9.6 原文(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"source","label":"原文","file":"8.31—9.6 原文(1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":385788,"date":"2026-08-31","range":"2026-08-31|2026-09-06","title":"More than 3,000 high street firms","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.31—9.6 原文(1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"reading","label":"精读","file":"8.31 精读 (1).pdf","ext":".pdf","bytes":344829,"date":"2026-08-31","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\8.31 精读 (1).pdf","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.31 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":57583,"date":"2026-08-31","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.31 检验题__阅读理解(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"},{"kind":"test","label":"检验题","file":"【福利】8.31检验题__完型填空(1).docx","ext":".docx","bytes":59349,"date":"2026-08-31","range":"","title":"","sourcePath":"D:\\外刊\\【福利】8.31检验题__完型填空(1).docx","raw":".cache\\periodical-raw2"}]};
